A||||16||Shaun41178||Civic EX, Probe GT, Mustang GT, and 3rd Gen Z28 Whew!!||||10||
Z||000000||Shaun41178||02-26-2000||05:05 PM||||Last night was awesome here in Ohio. I knew people would be bringing the cars out to cruise being around 50 degrees and the ground being nice and dry. I was right. They were coming out of the woodwork. Playing with a Probe and a Honda Civic for a bit and finally caught a light with the Civic. It was a late model Style with clear corners and a exhaust or at least a muffler cause it had the big tip. Not riced out though. He rolls down his window and says that I will kill him and that he only has a 1.6 liter. Well we still go anyway and sure enough I had 2 cars by 40 so I shut down. No purpose for taking it any higher when it has already been decided. He pulled up next to me and said I told you so. The guy was cool and gave me a thumbs up.<P>Probe was next and he came up from behind me full throttle buzzing like mad as he had a huge tip too. He had a passenger and a chick in the back. I find out later he was still in high school. So I tried to lay it down and catch up with him but he had too much of a head start so I couldn't catch him. We did catch a light though and I asked him what mods he had and he said headers gutted cat and the muffler and a stage 3 puck as he plans on adding nitrous later. While talking the chick starts waving to me and saying hi so I of course had to say hi back.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I should have worked my mojo and seen if she wanted to ride with me but oh well. So I tell him that I have a pulley and filter and have an auto tranny and ask him if he wants to go from the light. He agrees and I knew he was going to get creamed. With his FWD he is traction limited off the line plus the extra weight and when the light turned green I had about 2.5 cars at 50 or so so I shut down. We talked afterwards and he was a cool guy. <P>Next was a SN-95 Mustang GT. I noticed something different on his car then any other stang. He had like a checker flag sticker or something right next to his GT symbol on the front qtr panel. Does this mean anything to anybody? Anyway the only mod I could tell he had was an exhaust as it was quite loud so I asked if he wanted to go and he said sure. So we punch it from like a 10 mph roll and he pulls a car on me to 50. WTF???? Crazy thing is is that he had 2 other people in the car with him!!!! No freakin way. I aksed what he had done and he said nothing but I knew he had exhaust but to him he might have thought I meant forced induction of some kind and didn't count his exhaust as a mod or something. So I ask if he wants to go again and sure enough same outcome. This guy couldn't shift to save his life cause i heard him grinding it at every shift. I don't think it was his car even and that he was just driving it with the owner in the passenger seat. So I gave him the thumbs up and consented defeat. Damn this is one fast stang for sure or my bottle pressure was getting low or empty. <P>Later on some chicks in a SN-95 played a little but I couldn't get a good run in. Too much traffic. They were good lookin too. Its awesome when women want to play tag at least in my opinion. Don't see it everyday I guess.<P>Final race was against a 3rd gen Z28. It had a huge rear spoiler(Supra type) and a cowl induction hood and two huge chrome tips coming out the back. He had a strobe light going inside and all I could think of was Dork. I heard him rev it and it didn't sound too healthy so I thought I might have a chance as it looked intimidating. We are at a light to turn left and it goes green and we both take it slow and we get through the turn and he won't jump and I am goosing it and finally at about 25 he punches it so I lay into it too. 40......50...55 I start to pull a bit. I am at 65 and have a half car on the guy( I can see his bumper at my door and while I see his bumper at my door he is getting closer to my car. WTF!! This guy is trying to hit me!!! So I slam on the brakes and he does too and stays in his lane. Then he punches it about 2 cars back so I see him coming and I lay into it again but he has had a head start and passes me but by 60 I am reeling him and when I get to his rear bumper he starts cutting over in my lane so I can't pass and starts to hit his brakes and sh!t. AHHH so I am hard on the brakes again. I was steamed at this guy. Can't take losing so he has to act like he is going to hit me and cut me off. That guy was a pr!ck and ruined my whole night. I was having fun untill I ran into him. This is how accidents happen while racing cause @ssholes like this can't stand losing. Be carefull people and don't be like the guy in the camaro please.<P>The Car: <BR>85 Pontiac Fiero GT<BR>Drivetrain:<BR>2.8 V6 3.08 FD 3 spd auto <BR>MODS:<BR>Crane HI-6S ignition <BR>PS-91 Coil<BR>Accel 8.8 mm wires<BR>Throttle Body bypass<BR>K&N air filter<BR>Ported exhaust manifolds<BR>Underdrive Pulley<BR>NOS 70 hp shot<P>Best E.T. to Date: <BR>R/T:.707<BR>60': 1.895 on street tires, 215/60/r14 to be exact.<BR>330': 5.636<BR>1/8: 8.848 MPH: 75.60<BR>1000': 11.683<BR>1/4: 14.161 MPH: 89.18 <BR> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||02-26-2000||05:19 PM||||It's been a while since I have read any posts about your racing, Shaun. Now that the weather is gettting better and your 3.2 build up is under way I hope to read many more kills here.<P><B>Be safe and keep it between the ditches</B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||HF6582||02-26-2000||05:33 PM||||Shaun,<BR>The Mustangs with a checkered flag, would be on the 94Indy.<BR>The 94 Indy was only available as a Cobra.<BR>Still had the 5.0 in it.<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||02-26-2000||07:09 PM||||Nice kills, Shaun.  When you raced the Civic, were you running NOS?  Does the nos only kick in under WOT, or is it a steady flow when it's on? Later man...||||reg||12
Z||000004||BBBAD GT||02-26-2000||11:16 PM||||I could write a book on how to spot a 'ringer' 5.0, but you would probably be safe to assume the 96-98 Stangs (they had the vertical rear tailights) were the slowest and hardest to mod, except for the cobras.  1999's and up are a different story.  <P>Its not too uncommon to see a 10 sec street Stang (I have one) out driving around.  Personally, I never street race, too many stupid people out there.....but I wouldn't back down at the strip.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||02-27-2000||04:38 AM||||Hi Shaun,<P>What is a throttle body bypass?<BR>Did you have a type on yout 1/4 mile figures? 14.1 @ 89 MPH... 98 MPH maybe ???<P>David.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shaun41178||02-28-2000||06:09 PM||||GT basterd.  Yes I did use the nitrous against the civic althoguh I didn't have to.  I just wanted to show him how badly I could take him if I wanted.  Yes teh nitrous only kicks in under WOT.  I have a toggle switch wired to the TPS sensor and when the sensor goes to WOT it completes the ground and the fun begins.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The 14.1 @ 89 is not a typo.  The 89 is the mph that I ran.  My auto tranny is downright aweful once it hits third gear.  Come third gear and I have nothing left.  I am going to swap in a 3.33 tranny and install a higher stall TC and that should give me another few tenths and a few more mph easily right there.  New tranny and converter won't go in till my 3.2 goes in so it will be sometime this summer.||||reg||1
Z||000007||DRH||02-28-2000||07:00 PM||||Shaun, <P>Typical stock figures I've seen are in the 15.5 to 16.0 second range at 85 to 90 MPH. That means you are getting there about 1.5 seconds faster but at about the same speed. You must be pulling really good on the bottom end and loosing it on the top. Are you sure it's the tranny? Fuel pressure dropping maybe??? If you can get it to pull strong all the way I think you will be very pleased with your new ET.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Good luck, David.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||02-28-2000||11:32 PM||||After just saying checkered flag and mustang in the same sentance about 4 patrons of the shop (all mustang fodder) said Racecraft odds are that Mustang was equpped with a Racecraft either tuned or parts of thiers installed... or maybe hes gimp like the speds @ <A HREF="http://www.riceboypage.com" TARGET=_blank>www.riceboypage.com</A>  and just paid $20 for 2 stickers... the world may never know||||reg||1
Z||000009||GT Bastard||02-29-2000||12:01 AM||||Hey Shaun, I can vouch for the 3.33 tranny! I've got one, and it seems much snappier than my friends '86 SE with the std ratio.  Too bad we can't get 3.73's, but that might suck on the open road with no overdrive. ||||reg||6
Z||000010||Shaun41178||02-29-2000||05:22 PM||||Well I pulled my bottle today top see how much nitrous I have left.  Guess what.  It only had one pound left so I decided to just completely empty it and when I did the gas coming out wasn't even cold or foggy.  When nitrous comes out it is foggy so apparetnly there was not nitrous in the bottle.  I guess that is one good reason why I lost to that Mustang.  All I have to say is next time I see him he better be prepared to get his butt whooped as I am getting it refilled tomorrow.  Viva la Fiero||||reg||1
Z||000011||Capt Fiero||02-29-2000||07:06 PM||||How many pound bottle are you using, are you using a warmer in the trunk or is it warm enough, how much does each refill cost you.  How many average 1/4 mile runs can you get to a bottle.  I know the last question is trickey, because street runs are almost never a full quarter mile. And if you have the space to run over a quarter you never stop at just a quarter mile.<BR>Hope this does not fry your brain.<BR>David||||reg||1
Z||000012||1FST2M6||02-29-2000||10:00 PM||||My bottle usually lasts about 5 full runs before she falls on her face. On the street.. it lasts Friday and Saturday night. about 4 real hard pulls next to a vette or S/C MOOSEstang and then the rest on POS civics, preludes etc... I have a 10# bottle.   and yours Shaun...||||reg||1
Z||000013||Shaun41178||03-01-2000||04:18 PM||||I too have a 10 pound bottle.  I have gotten over 10 qtr mile runs on a bottle.  And they were all pretty consistent too.  In fact on some runs when the bottle wasn't as full I actually went faster.  Hmm makes me wonder.  Out on the street it will just about last forever at least that is what it seems since you don't almost ever go the full qtr mile at least in my area and most runs are just short stints.<P>I am not using a warmer on my bottle.  Why?  Cause I don't feel like shelling out the money for one.  It gets quite chilly here at night too.  What I do is put hot water bottles around my bottle and then cover it up wqith a nitrous bottle blanket.  Ok you caught me it isn't a real nos bottle blanket but a bed blanket that I put around the bottles and the nitrous bottle to keep in the heat.  It seems to work well and it is much cheaper too.  Nitrous costs me around $3-$3.50 a pound where I get it and today since my bottle was empty it cost exactly $35 to have it filled||||reg||1
Z||000014||Capt Fiero||03-01-2000||05:07 PM||||Thank you both, the reason that I am asking is that I have just been given 2 spare V-6 motors complet pan to intake. A spare tranny and tones of other goodies.  Both motors have bad or going bearings.  Not a big deal on the stand on thow 75$ into a new bottom end kit. Both have great compression and do not burn oil.  On top off all that I was given 2 spare sets of heads.  I am guessing that I can put all the parts together and make 2 good motors. Plus the 6cyl that I am driving.  You guys have given me some great info on what to do and use.  I already have the MSD ingition as well as some decent Wires 300ohm per foot 8.5mm Aurora's.    So hopefully buy the time that summer gets into full swing I will be out there running the real gas in my motor. YE HAW. 50hp shot to begin with. Oh and both my trannys are auto. The car is an 85GT.  It is taking me a while to get there but I will get there.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Uaana||03-02-2000||02:52 AM||||Are you guys running NOS on stock engines?<BR>I was alwasy told that doing that was a quick<BR>way to burn your rings and turn a decent running engine into a decent 300lb boat anchor.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Capt Fiero||03-03-2000||02:36 AM||||I am not running nos yet.  But from what I understand is, if you make sure not to lean out, you keep the timming just a bit retarded and do not run a shot that is more than 1/2 of your current hp, you should be fine.  Which means a 70hp shot regularly for a fresh rebuilt 2.8 and a 50hp for a well worked in 2.8.  It will make a bad motor worse, but no worse for it then say a turbo with 10lbs boost.    Anything that makes more power in an engine is going to be harder on it.  Nitrous is not a bad thing, if you understand it.  Ya back in the days of old when my dad was growing up they did not have the control over it like we do know and it blew alot of motors all to hell.  But from what I have learned and read. If you use it with some brains.  Almost any stock motor can get some help from it.  Mild to Wild depending on the condition of your motor or how well it has been built either stock or Forged everything.  Sorry for running this out so long.  Just trying to help someone else because everyone else has been helping me.  ||||reg||1
